{
  "name": "Jester's Fallen-Star Musket",
  "category": "combat",
  "concept": {
    "literalSynthesis": "A Jester-themed star musket paired with a fallen star: the musket identity frames the shot, while the fallen star supplies the actual ammunition and the small star that follows a hit.",
    "coreMechanic": "Fire one cursor-aimed, gravity-arcing ranged shot at the musket's source cadence. Each shot consumes selected fallen-star ammunition through native ammo handling. The shot can pierce up to three NPCs; each actual hit releases one lower-damage star that slowly homes toward nearby enemies. The primary projectile keeps the source's long-lived yellow glow. Its 31 base damage and three-hit potential preserve the musket's useful output, while the child star adds a modest follow-up rather than multiplying the shot into another full-strength attack. The weapon remains reusable; ammunition is its recurring cost.",
    "parentAContribution": "The Jester's Star Musket contributes the musket identity and its ranged, 31-damage, 32-tick use rhythm. Its purposeful role here is the reusable launcher and strong piercing primary shot; the new gravity arc and on-hit child are authored additions, not claims about its observed projectile.",
    "parentBContribution": "The Fallen Star contributes the actual fallen_star ammo category and celestial-star identity. The child star is a new authored follow-up; it is not presented as an observed Fallen Star ability.",
    "playerExperience": "Aim and fire at the source musket cadence. Each accepted shot uses the native fallen-star ammo selection and conservation rules. The shot arcs downward, may hit up to three NPCs, and each hit can create one weaker homing star. The weapon itself is reusable.",
    "plannedPlayerActions": [
      {
        "input": "primary_use",
        "intent": "Aim and fire a reusable musket shot using fallen-star ammunition; use the arcing, piercing shot and its weaker homing stars for ranged combat."
      }
    ]
  },
